# AGENTS

Research code for {{ project_display_name }}. SPEC.md says what the project studies, ARCHITECTURE.md where the code lives, REVIEW.md how changes are reviewed.

1. If `AGENTS.local.md` exists, read it at the start of every session and follow it (machines, storage paths, credentials). It is gitignored: never copy its contents into tracked files, commits or PRs.
2. If you are unsure, ask me first. If you cannot ask me, search the documentation. Do not guess.
3. Before writing experiment code, agree with me on what the experiment compares, its metric and its output, and write them into SPEC.md.
4. Use TDD: write tests before source code. Tests run on a CPU without model weights; mark a test that needs a GPU, weights or the network with `@pytest.mark.gpu`.
5. Use only the folders in ARCHITECTURE.md and put each file in its folder. Ask before creating a new folder.
6. Use uv: `uv sync`, `uv run pytest`, `uv run ruff check`.
7. One experiment is one config in `configs/` and one entry point in `scripts/`. Plot scripts read `results/` and save figures to `figs/` as PDF, not PNG.
8. Log incrementally: tee every print to stdout and to `logs/<experiment>/run.log`, and save partial results to `results/<experiment>/` after each completed condition.
9. Support checkpoint and resume: after each unit of work (example, config, condition), save progress to disk; on restart, skip finished units. A job can be preempted at any time.
10. Large intermediates that can be recomputed (cached activations, model checkpoints) go to the scratch path in `AGENTS.local.md`, not into the repo.
11. Wrap each long run in `notify_on_exit` from `src/{{ project_name_snake }}/notify.py`: one email when it finishes or fails, no progress emails.
12. Before starting work, check for an open PR for it and continue on its branch; otherwise start a new branch. Open PRs as drafts and keep them short. I merge.
13. Keep code clean and concise.
